From d5317bdc0ae0e2daecb3da180e2e18482ec8b9e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:17:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(memory): route remember/recall through kernel_memories +
 FTS5

Retires the flat JSONL memory-store: remember writes and recall reads now
go through kernel_memories (project-memory facade). recall uses FTS BM25
token-AND for queries and caps a no-query read to newest-N + a total count
(never a bare full dump). A legacy .forge/memory/notes.jsonl is imported
once on first use, then renamed. Adds project-memory.closeAll lifecycle
helper. Since insights already writes kernel_memories, its rows are now
recallable.

Issue: 9c8060f8-f4ec-47f4-b923-5e247c5bcdfd
